 "type": "hazard",
 "summary": "build_search_index.py \"unexpected token in shard-NNN.json\" means stale cache; rerun with --clear-cache",
 "content": "Running `python3 scripts/build_search_index.py` fails with \"index build failed: unexpected token in shard-000.json\" (exit 1) when var/cache/search/*.json shards were written by an older TOKENIZER version (the script's TOKENIZER constant, currently 3; stale shards had tokenizer 2). The message doesn't say it's a version mismatch. Fix: rerun with `--clear-cache`, which deletes the derived cache shards and rebuilds var/search/. Rerun it after any TOKENIZER bump.",
 "physical": [
  "scripts/build_search_index.py"
 ],
 "tags": [
  "search-index",
  "cache"
 ]
}
